AIM
To design and develop an online flowers and gifts ordering website using HTML, CSS, and JavaScript that allows users to browse gifts, select products, add items to a shopping cart, and place orders by entering delivery details.
ALGORITHM
1. Start the program.
2. Create an HTML page to display flowers and gifts with their prices.
3. Apply CSS to design the product cards and shopping cart.
4. Use JavaScript to display products and filter them by category.
5. Allow users to add products to the shopping cart.
6. Calculate and display the total price of the selected products.
7. Collect customer name and delivery date when placing an order.
8. Display the order confirmation message.
9. Stop the program.
HTML CODE — index.html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>BlossomGifts</title>
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="style.css">
</head>
<body>
    <header>
        <h1>BlossomGifts</h1>
        <p>Make Every Occasion Special</p>
    </header>

    <main>
        <section class="filters">
            <h2>Explore Our Gifts</h2>

            <select id="category" onchange="displayProducts()">
                <option value="all">All Categories</option>
                <option value="Flowers">Flowers</option>
                <option value="Gifts">Gifts</option>
                <option value="Cakes">Cakes</option>
            </select>
        </section>

        <div id="products" class="product-list"></div>

        <section class="cart">
            <h2>Shopping Cart</h2>
            <div id="cartItems"></div>
            <h3 id="total">Total: ₹0</h3>

            <h3>Delivery Details</h3>
            <input type="text" id="customer"
                   placeholder="Customer name">

            <input type="date" id="deliveryDate">

            <button onclick="placeOrder()">Place Order</button>
            <p id="message"></p>
        </section>
    </main>

    <footer>
        <p>&copy; 2026 BlossomGifts</p>
    </footer>

    <script src="script.js"></script>
</body>
</html>

